"A bar in 3/4 has a dotted half note. What else fits in the bar?": "a64257490f51",
"A dot after a note makes it longer by half of its own value. A half note is two beats, so a dotted half note is two plus one, three beats. A dotted quarter note is one and a half beats. There are rests, too. A rest is the absence of sound for a set length of time, and each kind is named for the note value it matches. A quarter rest lasts as long as a quarter note, and it is silent.": "19cd0c724e7a",
"A dot makes a note half again as long.": "b8136d40bef4",
